[Term]
id: CL:4307005
name: CB PLI GABA Ly6d Purkinje layer interneuron
def: "A Purkinje layer interneuron of the Mus musculus brain. It is distinguished from other cells in the brain by selective expression of Ly6d (Mmus), Kit (Mmus). It is distinguished from other CB PLI Gly-Gaba cells by expression of Ly6d. It is GABAergic. These cells are located in the Cerebellum, brain , in or close to the regions: arbor vitae, Interposed nucleus, Nodulus (X) . Reference transcriptomic data for this type can be found in the dataset/taxonomy - Yao et al. (2023), Whole Mouse Brain in cell set Cluster:5185 CB PLI Gly-Gaba_4." [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06812-z]
comment: Warning: Despite its name, CB PLI Gly-Gaba_4 does not secrete the neurotransmitter Gly, as assessed by expression of multiple marker genes.
